@inject Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptions<StoreOptions> Options
@{
    var store = Options.Value;
    ViewData["Title"] = "Subscription terms";
}

<p>These terms apply when you choose <strong>Subscribe</strong> for a product. They form part of our <a asp-action="Terms">terms of service</a>.</p>

<h2>How it works</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Subscription items cost @store.SubscriptionDiscountPercent% less than buying them one at a time.</li>
    <li>You choose how often each item is delivered: every 30, 60 or 90 days.</li>
    <li>
        Your subscription renews automatically at the price shown at checkout, plus any shipping charge shown there, until
        you cancel. We charge the payment method you used at checkout (your PayPal account or card), which PayPal stores
        securely for this purpose.
    </li>
    <li>Each renewal is charged on its renewal date and shipped as a new order.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Reminders</h2>
<p>
    We email you 3 days before every renewal with the date, the items and the amount, so you have time to make changes.
    You'll also get an email receipt each time a renewal is charged.
</p>

<h2>Skipping, pausing, changing and cancelling</h2>
<p>
    You can do all of these yourself at any time from <a asp-controller="Account" asp-action="Index">your account</a>.
    Sign in with your email address; we'll send you a sign-in link, no password needed. You can also email us at
    @store.ContactEmail.
</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Skip</strong> moves your next renewal back by one delivery period.</li>
    <li><strong>Pause</strong> stops renewals until you resume.</li>
    <li><strong>Change frequency</strong> switches between every 30, 60 or 90 days.</li>
    <li><strong>Cancel</strong> takes effect immediately and stops all future charges. There's no cancellation fee.</li>
</ul>
<p>
    Orders already charged before you cancel will still ship. If you meant to cancel before a renewal, email us before
    that order ships and we'll cancel and refund it.
</p>

<h2>If a payment fails</h2>
<p>
    If we can't charge your payment method on the renewal date, we'll email you and try again 2 days later. After 3
    unsuccessful attempts we pause your subscription and let you know. Nothing more is charged until you resume it.
</p>

<h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
<p>
    If we change these terms in a way that affects your subscription, we'll email you before the change applies to your
    next renewal.
</p>
